[h1]0.10 Land and Larder, for EU5 1.4[/h1]
0.10 is a big update and not save compatible: please start a new campaign. Read the [b]Change Notes[/b] tab for everything that changed, and the in-game Europedia for how it works.

Report bugs on Discord: [url=https://discord.gg/HgFd69Sv83]discord.gg/HgFd69Sv83[/url]

[h2]Prosper or Perish[/h2]
Prosper or Perish is a mod that tries to center Europa Universalis V gameplay more around the availability and production of food. One of the big growth bottlenecks of the era was food, and my goal is that every country's starting position flows naturally toward history-adjacent outcomes.

I follow three questions for every feature:
[list]
[*] Is the mechanic fun to manage for the player?
[*] Is it a concept that can be understood historically?
[*] Can the AI handle it?
[/list]

[h2]Food[/h2]
[img]https://janb1989.github.io/prosper-or-perish-constructor/assets/steam/0.10/food.jpg[/img]
[list]
[*] The food stored in each province is the key thing to keep an eye on: a full store makes people grow, an empty one makes them starve and leave.
[*] Food is no longer on the market, only trade goods are. Farms and Cookshops turn staples into Province Food, which stays in its province.
[*] Victuals are the one food that travels between markets: Granges pack a full province store, Victualling Yards pack staples from the market, and Taverns unpack them where food runs short.
[/list]

[h2]Arable Land[/h2]
[img]https://janb1989.github.io/prosper-or-perish-constructor/assets/steam/0.10/arable_land.jpg[/img]
[list]
[*] Population capacity is now the people a location's land can feed. Townsfolk house themselves; subsistence peasants and farms use the land.
[*] Land improvements such as Land Clearance, Drainage Ditches, Irrigated Fields, Qanats and Terraces win new land; every farm level takes some.
[*] The location view shows two bars, Land Usage against Land Capacity: townsfolk, subsistence peasants and farms against the land, and the land still open to improvements.
[/list]

[h2]A World Built from Real Data[/h2]
[img]https://janb1989.github.io/prosper-or-perish-constructor/assets/steam/0.10/navigable_rivers.jpg[/img]
[list]
[*] Every location's climate, vegetation, terrain, soil, fertility and rivers are rebuilt from geographic and historical data, and so are its farmland, its starting improvements and the output of every farmed good.
[*] More than a hundred great rivers carry ships inland, from the Rhine and the Volga to the Nile, the Ganges, the Yangtze and the Mississippi.
[*] Mountains, jungles, swamps and forests slow down hostile armies.
[/list]

[h2]Variable Harvests[/h2]
[img]https://janb1989.github.io/prosper-or-perish-constructor/assets/steam/0.10/harvest.jpg[/img]
Every September a new harvest raises or lowers the output of farmed goods, region by region. Grain and rice swing the most, herds and fish are spared. A good store gets a province through a bad year. You can turn it off in the game rules, even in a running game.

[h2]Buildings, Labor and Logistics[/h2]
[img]https://janb1989.github.io/prosper-or-perish-constructor/assets/steam/0.10/logistics.jpg[/img]
[list]
[*] RGOs can no longer be upgraded; more than 50 buildings replace them. The RGOs locations start with stay, for balance.
[*] Labor is a new good: the idle peasants of a market produce it, and nearly every building pays part of its costs in it.
[*] Logistics buildings (river boatmen, coastal shipping, carrier inns, caravanserais and more) raise market access where a location has more buildings than its land supports.
[*] Eight crop farms with four tiers each, manufacturing tiers, upgrades that keep their old recipes, and town rights to specialise in one good.
[/list]

[h2]A Smarter AI[/h2]
[list]
[*] The AI builds farms and food buildings where food runs short, and answers a shortage of goods by building supply and trading for it.
[*] Peace deals take connected land, so wars end without border gore, and nations let go of land they can never govern.
[*] Great powers plan more wars, and only AI countries with real colonial reach start colonial charters.
[/list]

[h2]Getting Started[/h2]
[list]
[*] Look at the game rules when you start: Variable Harvests, AI Food Consumption and Player Building Maintenance are the mod's settings.
[*] Open the Europedia at the top right. The Prosper or Perish pages explain every system, with live numbers from your own country.
[*] Try the map modes: Province Food Growth, Victuals Price, Farming Capacity, Navigable Rivers, Fertility, Soil Type and the local productivity of every good.
[*] Updates can break saves. Every version stays on GitHub, so you can keep a copy of the mod for a running campaign.
[/list]

